{"cues": [{"duration": 2.8, "start": 0.12, "text": "Hello again; today we sketch parabolas by hand."}, {"duration": 4.32, "start": 9.66, "text": "Our next curve in the family of conics is\nthe parabola."}, {"duration": 5.49, "start": 13.99, "text": "Slice a double cone with a plane that runs parallel\nto one of its slanted sides"}, {"duration": 5.93, "start": 19.48, "text": "and the cut you get never closes up, unlike the circle\nor the ellipse we met"}, {"duration": 1.56, "start": 25.41, "text": "in earlier lessons."}, {"duration": 5.33, "start": 26.97, "text": "You have drawn parabolas already, as graphs of quadratic\nfunctions such as y equals x squared,"}, {"duration": 3.149, "start": 32.3, "text": "so here we add the geometric definition."}, {"duration": 5.421, "start": 35.449, "text": "Pick one point, which we name the focus, and one line,\nwhich we name the directrix."}, {"duration": 4.439, "start": 40.87, "text": "The curve collects every point whose two distances agree."}, {"duration": 5.41, "start": 45.309, "text": "Put differently, measure from a point on the curve to\nthe focus, then measure straight across"}, {"duration": 3.561, "start": 50.719, "text": "to the directrix; the two numbers match."}, {"duration": 5.169, "start": 54.28, "text": "Compare the ellipse, where we add the distances to\ntwo special points and keep that total"}, {"duration": 2.68, "start": 59.449, "text": "fixed as the point moves."}, {"duration": 5.891, "start": 62.129, "text": "Algebraically a parabola is the graph of a quadratic,\nand some quadratics are easy to read,"}, {"duration": 7.95, "start": 68.02, "text": "like y equals x squared or a shifted copy written\nwith the square of x minus a number"}, {"duration": 1.62, "start": 75.97, "text": "plus a constant."}, {"duration": 5.52, "start": 77.59, "text": "Harder cases look like y equals minus x squared, minus\ntwo x, plus one."}, {"duration": 5.45, "start": 83.11, "text": "Written this way, the shifts and the stretch are hidden,\nso we cannot read them off"}, {"duration": 1.6, "start": 88.56, "text": "the formula directly."}, {"duration": 4.0, "start": 90.16, "text": "There are two good routes forward."}, {"duration": 6.47, "start": 94.16, "text": "Route one rewrites the formula into vertex form; route\ntwo keeps standard form and follows a checklist"}, {"duration": 5.5, "start": 100.63, "text": "that tells us where the turning point sits, which way\nthe curve opens, and which"}, {"duration": 2.75, "start": 106.13, "text": "extra points help us draw it."}, {"duration": 3.26, "start": 108.88, "text": "We will start with route one."}, {"duration": 2.59, "start": 112.14, "text": "It relies on the trick called completing the square."}, {"duration": 5.73, "start": 114.73, "text": "Completing the square turns the quadratic part into one\nsquared binomial, which exposes vertex"}, {"duration": 5.4, "start": 120.46, "text": "form, and from vertex form we can list each shift\nand stretch applied"}, {"duration": 5.149, "start": 125.86, "text": "to the plain curve y equals x squared."}, {"duration": 5.45, "start": 131.009, "text": "First we work it out for a general quadratic before\nwe use real numbers."}, {"duration": 6.451, "start": 136.459, "text": "Start from a x squared plus b x plus c; the goal\nis a times x minus h, squared,"}, {"duration": 7.6, "start": 142.91, "text": "plus k, where h and k are numbers we still need\nto find,"}, {"duration": 6.429, "start": 150.51, "text": "and where a, h and k tell us how the basic curve\nis stretched and moved,"}, {"duration": 1.3, "start": 156.939, "text": "which makes it simple to draw."}, {"duration": 5.36, "start": 158.239, "text": "Step one is to pull the factor a out of the two\nterms that contain x, leaving c"}, {"duration": 1.881, "start": 163.599, "text": "where it is for now."}, {"duration": 6.379, "start": 165.48, "text": "Inside the brackets the x squared term loses its a,\nand the x term becomes b over a times x."}, {"duration": 3.041, "start": 171.859, "text": "Step two completes the square."}, {"duration": 6.51, "start": 174.9, "text": "Take the coefficient of x inside the brackets, halve\nit, and square the result,"}, {"duration": 3.48, "start": 181.41, "text": "which gives b squared over four a squared."}, {"duration": 5.139, "start": 184.89, "text": "Adding that inside the brackets secretly adds a times\nthat amount to the whole expression,"}, {"duration": 6.91, "start": 190.029, "text": "because the factor a multiplies everything inside, so\nto keep the value unchanged"}, {"duration": 6.34, "start": 196.939, "text": "we take away b squared over four a outside the brackets,"}, {"duration": 2.21, "start": 203.279, "text": "and nothing about the function moves."}, {"duration": 5.67, "start": 205.489, "text": "Now the three terms inside form a perfect square, so\nwe can collapse them"}, {"duration": 4.131, "start": 211.159, "text": "into x plus b over two a, all squared."}, {"duration": 7.0, "start": 215.29, "text": "Writing that as x minus the quantity negative b over two\na shows the shape we wanted:"}, {"duration": 3.199, "start": 222.29, "text": "the vertex form."}, {"duration": 4.87, "start": 225.489, "text": "Here h equals negative b over two a, and k is whatever\nconstant is left outside, and together they mark the vertex;"}, {"duration": 2.05, "start": 230.359, "text": "a still sets the stretch."}, {"duration": 7.771, "start": 232.409, "text": "Back to our example: a is negative one, b is negative\ntwo and c is one, so h and k come out"}, {"duration": 8.699, "start": 240.18, "text": "as negative one and two, putting the vertex at the point\nnegative one, two."}, {"duration": 6.381, "start": 248.879, "text": "Because a is negative one, the curve opens downward and\nhas the same width as x squared."}, {"duration": 5.509, "start": 255.26, "text": "That is the whole path from standard form to vertex form,\nand vertex form"}, {"duration": 1.781, "start": 260.769, "text": "is quick to sketch."}, {"duration": 4.95, "start": 262.55, "text": "With practice you can skip the general derivation and\nrepeat the same moves"}, {"duration": 2.02, "start": 267.5, "text": "directly on the numbers."}, {"duration": 5.92, "start": 269.52, "text": "Factor a from the x terms, complete the square, remember\nto multiply the added amount by a"}, {"duration": 6.74, "start": 275.44, "text": "when you balance it outside, collapse the square, and\nread off the vertex."}, {"duration": 4.46, "start": 285.04, "text": "Now for route two, where we keep the standard form and\nwork through a checklist."}, {"duration": 4.67, "start": 289.51, "text": "Step one: decide which way the curve opens, up"}, {"duration": 1.48, "start": 294.18, "text": "or down."}, {"duration": 4.58, "start": 295.66, "text": "That depends only on the sign of the leading coefficient a."}, {"duration": 3.049, "start": 300.24, "text": "A positive a gives a curve that opens up."}, {"duration": 2.141, "start": 303.289, "text": "A negative a gives one that opens down."}, {"duration": 4.89, "start": 305.43, "text": "Our a is negative one, so this curve opens downward."}, {"duration": 2.439, "start": 310.32, "text": "Step two: locate the vertex."}, {"duration": 5.831, "start": 312.759, "text": "Its x coordinate is negative b divided by two a, which\nfor our numbers is"}, {"duration": 6.479, "start": 318.59, "text": "that is, minus negative two, divided by twice negative one,"}, {"duration": 2.391, "start": 325.069, "text": "and that equals negative one."}, {"duration": 5.19, "start": 327.46, "text": "Next we substitute x equals negative one into the formula\nto get the matching y value,"}, {"duration": 3.019, "start": 332.65, "text": "which works out to two here."}, {"duration": 4.911, "start": 335.669, "text": "So the turning point really is negative one, two."}, {"duration": 5.399, "start": 340.58, "text": "To add detail we can look for the points where the\ngraph meets each axis."}, {"duration": 5.521, "start": 345.979, "text": "The x intercepts are where y is zero, so we set the\nformula equal to zero"}, {"duration": 3.539, "start": 351.5, "text": "and solve that equation for x."}, {"duration": 5.321, "start": 355.039, "text": "For this quadratic the roots are not whole numbers, so\nwe reach for the quadratic formula,"}, {"duration": 4.75, "start": 360.36, "text": "which an earlier lesson covers if you want a refresher\non"}, {"duration": 1.89, "start": 365.11, "text": "the steps involved."}, {"duration": 7.03, "start": 367.0, "text": "Substituting a, b and c gives two roots, and rounding\neach one to one decimal place"}, {"duration": 5.71, "start": 374.03, "text": "is accurate enough to place them on a sketch."}, {"duration": 4.959, "start": 379.74, "text": "The y intercept is easier: it is the height of the curve"}, {"duration": 5.391, "start": 384.699, "text": "at x equals zero, where the graph crosses the vertical axis."}, {"duration": 3.77, "start": 390.09, "text": "Substituting zero gives one."}, {"duration": 6.61, "start": 393.86, "text": "Finally we can draw the axis of symmetry, the vertical\nline x equals negative b over two"}, {"duration": 4.159, "start": 400.47, "text": "a, as a check on the rest."}, {"duration": 5.641, "start": 404.629, "text": "With the vertex, the intercepts and the axis in hand we\nhave all we need"}, {"duration": 5.57, "start": 410.27, "text": "for a fair sketch of the curve."}, {"duration": 5.12, "start": 415.84, "text": "So we now know several ways to graph a parabola, even one\nthat starts in an awkward form."}, {"duration": 6.359, "start": 420.96, "text": "Vertex form lets us apply shifts and stretches, and\nstandard form can be handled"}, {"duration": 6.44, "start": 427.319, "text": "by completing the square or by computing key points\none at a time."}, {"duration": 6.56, "start": 433.76, "text": "Parabolas also show up in mechanics: a thrown ball\nfollows one when we ignore air resistance."}, {"duration": 4.36, "start": 440.32, "text": "That is a story for another lesson, because one more\nconic still waits"}, {"duration": 1.351, "start": 444.699, "text": "for us after this."}, {"duration": 2.11, "start": 446.05, "text": "Before moving on, try the practice questions."}], "video_id": "hvJkCMzFiX8"}